        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 26 at 2:58AM AKDT until September 27 at 5:00AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>Southeast Alaska Inside Waters from Dixon Entrance to Skagway

Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Sea forecasts represent the average of the highest
one-third of the combined windwave and swell height.

.TODAY...S wind 15 kt. Seas building to 4 ft. Near ocean
entrances, seas 4 ft building to 8 ft. Rain.
.TONIGHT...S wind 15 kt increasing to 25 kt late. Seas 4 ft,
except 8 ft near ocean entrances. Rain.
.SUN...S wind 25 kt. Seas 5 ft, except 10 ft near ocean
entrances. Rain.
.SUN NIGHT...S wind 25 kt. Gusts to 40 kt. Seas 6 ft, except
11 ft near ocean entrances. Rain.
.MON...S wind 15 kt. Seas 3 ft.
.TUE...S wind 15 kt. Seas 3 ft.
.WED...SE wind 10 kt. Seas 3 ft.
</description>
